# Versioning

MailGent is **0.1.x alpha** until v1. Follow global SemVer (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`).

## Version bump = CHANGELOG entry (same commit)

**Never bump `MARKETING_VERSION` without updating root `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.**

1. Add a `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section at the top (below the title blurb).
2. Group bullets under `### Added`, `### Fixed`, `### Changed`, or `### Breaking`.
3. One section per release; do not edit past sections except typos.

Backfill missing history when you discover a gap (as with 0.1.0–0.1.3 before `CHANGELOG.md` existed).

## Files to keep in sync

| File | Field |
|------|-------|
| `project.yml` | `MARKETING_VERSION`, `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` |
| `MailGent.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` | regenerate via `xcodegen generate` after `project.yml` |
| `README.md` | **full** update — see below (not headline-only) |
| `PRIVACY.md` | `This X.Y.Z alpha binary…` (+ behavior blurb when the release changes privacy-relevant flows) |
| GitHub Release **title** | `X.Y.Z alpha` (pre-release until v1) |
| Git tag | `vX.Y.Z` (semver only — no `-alpha` suffix) |
| About window | `Version X.Y.Z alpha (build)` |
| Menu-bar version label | `vX.Y.Z` (compact; stage in About / release title) |
| `MailStore/Sources/LoopbackMCPServer.swift` | MCP `initialize` → `serverInfo.version` (semver only) |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | new top section for the bump |

### README (required on every bump)

**Never** bump with only the `**X.Y.Z alpha**` headline changed. In the **same commit**, update `README.md` fully:

1. Headline → `**X.Y.Z alpha**`
2. **## Features** — fold every user-facing item from that version’s `CHANGELOG.md` into the matching subsection (`Local mail`, `Agents`, `Grants`, `Ask`, `Rules`, `Leak guard`, `Access log`, `Drafts`). Add a subsection only when a new capability cluster appears. Keep bullets plain and scannable; do not leave shipped features out.
3. Tool lists / Settings callouts / other README claims that the release changed
4. Cross-check against `CHANGELOG` Added / Fixed / Changed / Breaking before closeout

Increment `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` on every release build.

## Git

- Do not land versioned work on `main` — branch `feat/…` or `fix/…` first.
- Tag the release commit `vX.Y.Z` when shipping.
- Docs/chore/internal-only: no version bump, no CHANGELOG entry.

## Tags vs GitHub Releases (alpha until v1)

All **0.1.x** ships as **pre-release alpha**. Same semver everywhere in code; **alpha** appears in user-facing titles only.

| Surface | Format | Example |
|---------|--------|---------|
| Git tag | `vX.Y.Z` | `v0.1.8` |
| GitHub Release **title** | `X.Y.Z alpha` | `0.1.8 alpha` |
| GitHub **pre-release** | always checked | — |
| DMG filename | `MailGent-X.Y.Z.dmg` | `MailGent-0.1.8.dmg` |
| `MARKETING_VERSION` / MCP / bundle | `X.Y.Z` | `0.1.8` |

**Do not** put `-alpha` on new git tags (legacy exception: `v0.1.0-alpha.1` — first alpha; keep the tag, title is `0.1.0 alpha`).

Workflow sets release title from the tag: strip leading `v`, append ` alpha`. Release notes start with that version’s `CHANGELOG.md` section (`Scripts/release/notes.sh`), then the install notes in `.github/RELEASE_BODY.md`.
